{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to require passwords of at least 12 characters using at least three character classes. The policy survived a full node restart; services, administrative access, OS release, kernel, security controls, and protected account data remained healthy and unchanged.","actions_performed":["Added /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/50-local-password-policy.conf with minlen=12, minclass=3, and enforce_for_root.","Verified short and two-class passwords are rejected, while passwords using exactly three classes are accepted.","Validated the PAM/authselect configuration and real passwd credential-change behavior.","Removed the temporary test identity and secrets; restored exact account-database checksums.","Restarted node1 safely and verified a changed boot ID, recovered services, persistent policy behavior, and preserved data.","Installed or upgraded no packages; retained RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Minimum password length of 12 characters","command_ids":["cmd-256863efa0f54e82","cmd-0aa3c40694f34a5a","cmd-8267782ecf624ea6"],"summary":"The durable policy specifies minlen=12, and 11-character candidates were rejected before and after restart."},{"requirement":"At least three character classes","command_ids":["cmd-256863efa0f54e82","cmd-0aa3c40694f34a5a","cmd-8267782ecf624ea6","cmd-238d0df50ccd4b8b"],"summary":"The policy specifies minclass=3; two-class candidates were rejected and an exactly-three-class candidate was accepted after restart."},{"requirement":"Policy enforced through the installed PAM password stack","command_ids":["cmd-ea143118e4644959","cmd-6c2259e6c9e7486e","cmd-36dd4132956f4917","cmd-4d359ef6ab31489c"],"summary":"PAM invokes pam_pwquality; noncompliant attempts preserved the prior credential while a compliant password changed it."},{"requirement":"Preserve account data and remove test artifacts","command_ids":["cmd-bc7873cf2e5f419d","cmd-0b149b22c40e4501","cmd-4bf705022bce4950"],"summary":"Temporary identity and secrets were removed, no residue remained, and passwd/group/shadow/gshadow checksums exactly matched the baseline."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release, kernel, and compatible software","command_ids":["cmd-d403ca094cb24a96","cmd-09dab7afa5bf431c","cmd-4bf705022bce4950"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0, kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64, and existing PAM/libpwquality/authselect packages remained installed without upgrades."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ff82f1068cec4b19","cmd-23db50d68c7d445c","cmd-68279a7973d94a09","cmd-09dab7afa5bf431c","cmd-8267782ecf624ea6"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID 050a5b4c-6c7b-42ad-957a-b6a41a0d34db was captured, reboot acknowledged, new boot ID b15398f5-0f20-478d-969e-c21d19f51e5b proved restart, and SSH, chrony, policy, PAM, protected data, and behavioral enforcement recovered."}]}
